Implement the Linux side of the texture-preload memory throttle.

The concurrent texture loader in Player::Player() gates each decode on the
amount of available physical memory (3x the estimated GPU size of the image),
but only on Windows: the Linux side is a 'TODO implement for other platforms'
that unconditionally reports memory as available. On a Pi 5 this means one
full-size decode per core at all times, whatever the table weighs; with
overcommit, allocations never fail (so the resizeOnLowMem fallback never
triggers either) and the OOM killer takes the process down instead -- a heavy
table freezes the machine mid-load.

Implement the check with MemAvailable from /proc/meminfo rather than the
sysinfo() sketch the TODO suggests: freeram does not count the reclaimable
page cache, which holds most of the 'free' memory right after streaming a
table file from disk, and would throttle the load down to nothing.

Same as upstream's Windows logic, the check only delays a decode while
another is in flight (nLoadInProgress == 0 loads unconditionally), so
progress is guaranteed and a mis-read of /proc/meminfo (availKB == 0) simply
restores the old behavior.

Signed-off-by: Adrien Beudin <beudbeud@gmail.com>

--- a/src/core/player.cpp	2026-07-18 18:43:34.619564876 +0200
+++ b/src/core/player.cpp	2026-07-18 18:43:54.341168780 +0200
@@ -607,11 +607,17 @@
                      statex.dwLength = sizeof(statex);
                      GlobalMemoryStatusEx(&statex);
                      readyToLoad = statex.ullAvailPhys > neededMem;
+                  #elif defined(__linux__)
+                     // MemAvailable, unlike sysinfo()'s freeram, accounts for the
+                     // reclaimable page cache, which holds most of the 'free' memory
+                     // right after streaming a big table file from disk.
+                     size_t availKB = 0;
+                     std::ifstream meminfo("/proc/meminfo");
+                     for (string l; std::getline(meminfo, l);)
+                        if (sscanf(l.c_str(), "MemAvailable: %zu", &availKB) == 1)
+                           break;
+                     readyToLoad = (availKB == 0) || (availKB * 1024 > neededMem);
                   #else
-                     // TODO implement for other platforms
-                     // struct sysinfo memInfo;
-                     // sysinfo(&memInfo);
-                     // readyToLoad = memInfo.freeram > neededMem;
                      readyToLoad = true;
                   #endif
                }
